# The first invitation is a relation, not a license

Hati Suci is the first invited community because the enquiry already has a
member inside it. That is a genuine relationship door. It is not a shortcut
around the community's own answer.

Hati Suci's Satsang circle holds both recognized roles: it receives and
witnesses the invitation, and it is the circle authorized to select and
approve the first material. The initiating member reports both roles.

The body's existing Satsang protocol fits the receiving role: any question is
welcome; affirmation, dissent, and silence are all retained; no single witness
decides for the circle. A proposal may survive the circle without erasing the
dissent that accompanied it.

Authority names who may answer; it is not the answer. Satsang has now selected
Giles' "The Light Hubs" as its first exact material. The supplied surface is
identified by hash. The initiating member now also reports Giles' scoped
permission, while the absence of a direct signed author artifact stays visible.

The initiating member can truthfully say:

    I am a member.
    I am bringing this invitation.

The initiating member can now also truthfully say:

    The Light Hubs is the first selected material.

The initiating member can now report that Giles permits:

    public quotation and reproduction
    translation
    open-AI reasoning and training use
    attribution as "Giles"
    continuing revision or withdrawal

That is a member-witnessed grant, not a direct signed artifact and not a
permission broader than its recorded scope. The initiating member has now
answered the separate Hati Suci boundary query with `none`: no additional
sacred, cultural, or community-use restriction is reported.

The executable pilot currently rests on an actionable `node` arm:

    nothing  no relationship door has been observed
    0        the community or one of its terms declines
    1        the community and every named term confirm
    node     Satsang receives a concrete next query with reply arms

The exact-material, scoped-permission, and cultural-boundary actions have been
answered. The current node now asks:

    What benefit or reciprocity, if any, should return from use?

Its response envelope is:

    nothing  no return or reciprocity statement has been observed
    0        Satsang declines use without an acceptable return
    1        Satsang records "none" or the exact benefit/return
    node     Satsang proposes a precise reciprocity arrangement

After that answer, the next unresolved term becomes the next action. The nine
ordered terms are:

    exact text or item — The Light Hubs selected
    member-witnessed selection and scoped author permission — recorded
    cultural or access restrictions — none recorded
    attribution and translator credit — "Giles" recorded
    translation and transliteration permission — recorded
    downstream and AI use — recorded
    benefit and reciprocity — current action
    withdrawal and removal — recorded
    freshness and review date

The community may answer `yes`, `no`, offer no observation, or propose another
shape. Silence makes no claim. A declined term is not averaged away by eight
confirmed terms. Withdrawal stays possible after an initial yes.

Even a complete 1 from this invitation only opens the source-registry door.
The exact edition, rights, source bytes, attribution, and fresh witness still
have to pass there. No Hati Suci text enters merely because Hati Suci was
first to be invited.

## Human permission and selection-receipt draft

To Giles and the Hati Suci Satsang circle,

Satsang has selected "The Light Hubs" as Hati Suci's first material for a
small, open framework that asks fundamental questions across languages while
preserving source, viewpoint, uncertainty, and consent.

The exact supplied transcription is identified by its SHA-256 fingerprint; its
full body has not been placed into immutable Git history.

The initiating member reports that Giles permits quotation/republication,
translation, open-AI reasoning/training, attribution as "Giles", and continuing
revision/withdrawal. Please now record:

    what benefit, if any, should return to Giles, Hati Suci, or the Light Hubs
    the review date or cadence
    which revocable carrier may hold the complete transmission

`Yes`, `no`, no observed answer, and `we propose these conditions` are all
complete responses. Silence makes no claim. A first permission does not become
permanent or broader than its recorded scope.

This reuses the body's older consent split: a member can introduce a friend,
but only the friend can open their own memory. Here, the initiating member can
introduce the enquiry to the recognized Satsang circle, but only the
community's own accepted process can open its shared materials.
